G1709.def:
ἐν-πνέω, -ῶ
(Rec. ἐμπ-, see: ἐν) [in LXX: Deutéronome 20:16, Josué 10:28 ff. Josué 11:11, 14 (ptcp. neut., for נֶפֶשׁ, נְשָׁמָה), Wis.15:11 * ;] 
__1. to breathe on. 
__2. to breathe; 
__(a) absol.; 
__(b) with genitive part.: figuratively, ἀπειλῆς κ. φόνου, Actes 9:1.†

G1715.def:
ἔμ-προσθεν 
adv. 
of place (in cl. also of time), 
[in LXX chiefly for עֳנִי ;] 
__1. adverbially, before, in front: Luc 19:28; εἰς τὸ ἔ., Luc 19:4; opposite to ὄπισθεν, Apocalypse 4:6; opposite to τὰ ὀπίσω, τὰ ἔ., Philippiens 3:13. 
__2. As prep., before; 
__(a) in front of: Matthieu 5:24 6:2 7:6 11:10 27:29, Luc 5:19 7:27 14:2, Jean 3:28 10:4, Apocalypse 19:10 22:8; 
__(b) in the presence of: Matthieu 27:11, Galates 2:14, 1 Thessaloniciens 1:3 2:19 3:9 3:13; ὁμολουεῖν, ἀρνεῖσθαι (Dalman, Words, 210), Matthieu 10:32, 36 26:70, Luc 12:8; in forensic sense, Matthieu 25:32 27:11, Luc 21:36, Actes 18:17, 2 Corinthiens 5:10, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:19, I Jn 3:19; εὐδοκία (θέλημά) ἐστι ἔ. θεοῦ (a targumic formula; Dalman, Words, 211), Matthieu 11:26 18:14, Luc 10:21; 
__(with) in the sight of: Matthieu 5:16 6:1 17:2 23:14, Marc 2:12 9:2, Luc 19:27, Jean 12:37, Actes 10:4; 
__(d) of rank and dignity (Dem., Plat., al.; LXX, Genèse 48:20): Jean 1:15, 30.†

G1722.def:
ἐν, 
prep, (the most frequently of all in NT), with dative (= Heb. בְּ, Lat. in, with abl.). 
__I. Of place, with dative of thing(s), of person(s), in, within, on, at, by, among: ἐν τ. πόλει, Luc 7:37; τ. οφθαλμῷ, Matthieu 7:3; τ. κοιλίᾳ, Matthieu 12:40; τ. ὄρει, 2 Pierre 1:18; τ. θρόνῳ, Apocalypse 3:21; τ. δεξιᾷ τ. θεοῦ, Romains 8:34; ἐν ἡμῖν Abbott-Smith has ὑμῖν., Luc 1:1; of books, ἐν τ. βιβλίῳ, Galates 3:10; τ. νόμῳ, Matthieu 12:5, al.; ἐν τοῖς τ. Πατρός, in my Father's house (RV; cf. M, Pr., 103), Luc 2:49; trop., of the region of thought or feeling, ἐν τ. καρδίᾳ (-αις), Matthieu 5:28, 2 Corinthiens 4:6, al.; τ. συνειδήσεσιν, 2 Corinthiens 5:11; after verbs of motion, instead of εἰς (constructio praegnans, a usage extended in late Gk. beyond the limits observed in cl.; cf. Bl., §41, 1; M, Th., 12), ἀποστέλλω . . . ἐν, Matthieu 10:16. δέδωκεν ἐν τ. χειρί (cf. τιθέναι ἐν χερσί, Hom., Il., i, 441, al.), Jean 3:35; id. after verbs of coming and going (not in cl.), εἰσῆλθε, Luc 9:46; ἐξῆλθεν, Luc 7:17. 
__II. Of state, condition, form, occupation, etc.: ἐν ζωῇ, Romains 5:10; ἐν τ. θανάτῳ, 1 Jean 3:14; ἐν πειρασμοῖς, 1 Pierre 1:6; ἐν εἰρήνῃ, Marc 5:25; ἐν δόξῃ, Philippiens 4:19; ἐν πραΰτητι, Jacques 3:13; ἐν μυστηρίῳ, 1 Corinthiens 2:7; ἐν τ. διδαχῇ, Marc 4:2; of a part as contained in a whole, ἐν τ. ἀμπέλῳ, Jean 15:4; ἐν ἑνὶ σώματι, Romains 12:4; of accompanying objects or persons (simple dative in cl.), with, ἐν αἵματι, Hébreux 9:25; ἐν δέκα χιλιάσιν, Luc 14:31 (cf. Ju 14, Actes 7:14); similarly (cl.), of clothing, armour, arms, ἐν στολαῖς, Marc 12:38; ἐν ἐσθῆτι λαμπρᾷ, Jacques 2:2; ἐν μαξαίρῃ, Luc 22:49; ἐν ῥάβδῳ, 1 Corinthiens 4:21 (cf. ἐν τόξοις, Xen., Mem., 3, 9, 2); of manner (cl.), ἐν τάχει (= ταχέως), Luc 18:8 (cf. Bl., §41, 1); of spiritual influence, ἐν πνεύματι, Romains 8:9; ἐν π. ἀκαθάρτῳ, Marc 1:23; of the mystical relation of the Christian life and the believer himself, to God and Christ (cf. ICC, Ro., 160f.; Mayor on Ju 1; M, Pr., 103): ἐν Χριστῷ, Romains 3:24, 6:11, 1 Corinthiens 3:1, 4:10, 2 Corinthiens 12:2, Galates 2:17, Éphésiens 6:21, Colossiens 4:7, 1 Thessaloniciens 4:16, al. 
__III. Of the agent, instrument or means (an extension of cl. ἐν of instr.—see LS, see word Ill—corresponding to similar use of Heb. בְּ), by, with: ἐν ὑμῖν κρίνεται ὁ κόσμος (= cl. παρά, C. dative), 1 Corinthiens 6:2; ἐν τ. ἄρχοντι τ. δαιμονίων, Matthieu 9:34; ἐν αἵματι, Hébreux 9:22; ἐν ὕδατι, Matthieu 3:11, al.; ἐν μαχαίρᾳ ἀποκτενεῖ (cf. the absol. ἐν μ., ἐν ῥάβδῳ, supr., II, which some would classify here), Apocalypse 13:10 (cf. 6:8). Allied to this usage and distinctly Semitic are the following: ἠγόρασας . . . ἐν τ. αἵματι σου (cf. BDB, see word בְּ, III, 3), Apocalypse 5:9; ὁμολογεῖν ἐν (= Aram. אודי בּ; cf. McNeile on Mt, I.with; M, Pr., 104), Matthieu 10:32, Luc 12:8; ὀμνύναι ἐν (= cl. accusative, so Jacques 5:12), Matthieu 5:34, al.; also at the rate of, amounting to, Marc 4:8 (WH; vv. ll., εἰς, ἒν), Actes 7:14 (LXX). 
__IV. Of time, 
__(a) in or during a period: ἐν τ. ἡμέρᾳ (νυκτί), Jean 11:9, al.; ἐν σαββάτῳ, Matthieu 12:2, al.; ἐν τῷ μεταξύ, meanwhile, Jean 4:31; 
__(b) at the time of an event: ἐν τ. παρουσίᾳ, 1 Corinthiens 15:23; ἐν τ. ἀναστάσει, Matthieu 22:28; 
__(with) with art. inf., 
__(α) present (so sometimes in cl., but not as in NT = ἕως; V. M, Pr., 215), while: Matthieu 13:4, Marc 6:48, Galates 4:18, al.; 
__(β) aor., when, after: Luc 9:36, al.; 
__(d) within (cl.): Matthieu 27:40, 
__V. In composition: (1) meaning: (a) with adjectives, it signifies usually the possession of a quality, as ἐνάλιος, ἐν́δοξος; (b) with verbs, continuance in (before ἐν) or motion into (before εἰς), as ἐμμένω, ἐμβαίνω. (ii) Assimilation: ἐν becomes ἐμ- before β, μ, π, φ, ψ; ἐγ- before γ, κ, ξ, χ; ἐλ- before λ. But in the older MSS of NT, followed by modern editions, assimilation is sometimes neglected, as in ἐνγράφω, ἐγκαινίζω, etc.

G1764.def:
ἐν-ίστημι 
[in LXX: 4Ki.13:6 A (עֶמְדָּה), 3Ki.12:24, 1Es.5:47 Esther 9:6, Esther 3:13, 1; 4Ma.9.1-32 * ;] 
to place in; in pf., plpf., 2 aor. and in mid., intrans.; 
__(a) to be at hand, impend, threaten: 2 Timothée 3:1; 
__(b) to be present: 2 Thessaloniciens 2:2 (but see Thayer, see word); pf. ptcp., present: 1 Corinthiens 7:26, Galates 1:4, Hébreux 9:9; pl., Romains 8:38, 1 Corinthiens 3:22 (Cremer, 3O9).†

G1785.def:
ἐντολή, -ῆς, ἡ
(ἐντέλλω, which see), [in LXX chiefly for מִצְוָה; in pl. frequently in Pss for פִּקּוּד ;] 
__1. generally, a charge, injunction, order, command: Luc 15:29, Jean 10:18 11:57 12:49-50 14:31, Actes 17:15, Colossiens 4:10; ἐ. σαρκίνη, Hébreux 7:16, 18 
__2. Esp. of religious precepts and commandments; 
__(a) of God's commandments: in OT, Matthieu 15:3 22:36, 38 22:40 Mk 7:8-9; Marc 10:5, 19 12:28, 31 Éphésiens 2:15, Hébreux 9:19; esp. of the decalogue, Matthieu 5:19 19:17, Marc 10:19, Luc 18:20 23:56, Romains 7:8-13 13:9, Éphésiens 6:2; of God's command­ments in general, Luc 1:6, 1 Corinthiens 7:19, 1 Jean 2:3-8 Jn 3:22-24 Jn 4:21 Jn 5:2-3, Apocalypse 12:17 14:12; collectively, ἡ ἐ. (cf. τ. ἔργον τ. θεοῦ, Jean 6:29), 1 Timothée 6:14, 2 Pierre 2:21 3:2; 
__(b) of things commanded Christ by the Father: Jean 12:49-50 14:31 15:10; 
__(with) of the precepts of Christ: Jean 13:34 14:15, 21 15:10, 12, 1 Corinthiens 14:37. 
__3. Phrases: before ἵνα, Jean 13:34 15:12, 1 Jean 3:23 Jn 4:21, 2Jn.6; ἐντολὴν (ὰς) παραβαίνειν, Matthieu 15:3; ἀκυροῦν, Matthieu 15:6 Rec.; τηρεῖν, Matthieu 19:17 Jean 15:10, al.; ποιεῖν, 1 Jean 5:2; διδόναι, Jean 11:57; λαμβάνειν, Jean 10:18, 2Jn.4; ἔχειν, Jean 14:21, Hébreux 7:5; ἐ. καὶ δικαιώματα, Luc 1:6; ἐντολαὶ ἀνθρώπων (of Jewish tradition), Tite 1:14; i. καινή, Jean 13:34, 1 Jean 2:7, 2Jn.5.†
